---
// Two fact tables (sales and returns) sharing the same conformed dimensions, and drilling across them.
---
<figure class="cfd">
  <div class="cfd-grid">
    <div class="cfd-fact">fact_sales<span>one row per order line</span></div>
    <div class="cfd-dims">
      <div class="cfd-dim">dim_product<span>product_key, category, department</span></div>
      <div class="cfd-dim">dim_date<span>date_key, month, fiscal year</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cfd-fact">fact_returns<span>one row per returned item</span></div>
  </div>
  <ol class="cfd-steps">
    <li>Sum <b>fact_sales</b> by department.</li>
    <li>Count <b>fact_returns</b> by the same department column.</li>
    <li>Join the two small results on department ("drill across").</li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>Both facts use the same dimension tables, with the same keys and the same labels, so their totals line up row for row. Never join the two fact tables to each other directly.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style is:inline>
.cfd { margin: 20px 0; }
.cfd-grid { display: grid; gap: 8px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; text-align: center; }
@media (min-width: 560px) { .cfd-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr 1fr; align-items: center; } }
.cfd-fact, .cfd-dim { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 8px 10px; background: var(--surface); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 14px; }
.cfd-fact { border: 2px solid var(--accent); }
.cfd-dim { background: var(--accent-soft); }
.cfd-dims { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
.cfd-fact span, .cfd-dim span { display: block; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }
.cfd-steps { margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 22px; font-size: 14px; }
.cfd figcaption { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
